// array_new_jagged.tk -- `T[][]` is a type teko reads (D100), but the
// ALLOCATOR that would fill its rows is not taught: `new i64[3][]` would
// write three zeroed pointer slots into a row typed plain `i64[]`, and the
// rows of a jagged array come from a store today. The `[]` right after a
// fresh `new i64[3]` used to reach the core's own "expression expected", with
// no `teko:` prefix and in no catalogue; it is refused here instead.
//
// `new i64[3][0]` -- an INDEX over a fresh array -- keeps its meaning
// (`tests/surface_array_heap.tk`).

// expect-refuse: teko: `new T[n][]` is not taught yet
// expect-refuse-line: 15

i64 main() {
    i64[][] g = new i64[3][];
    return 0;
}
